{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q415950","formula":"Cu(UO₂)₂(SO₄)₂(OH)₂·8H₂O","hill":"CuH18O22S2U2","elements":["H","O","S","Cu","U"],"composition":{"H":18.0,"O":22.0,"S":2.0,"U":2.0,"Cu":1.0},"names":{"en":"Johannite","uk":"Йоганніт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Johannite is a rare uranium sulfate mineral. It crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with the chemical composition Cu[UO2(OH)SO4]2·8H2O. It crystallizes in the triclinic system and develops only small prism or thin to thick tabular crystals, usually occurs as flaky or spheroidal aggregates and efflorescent coatings. Its color is emerald-green to apple-green and its streak is pale green.","uk":"Йогані́т — мінерал, водний сульфат урану та міді шаруватої будови."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q415950","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%99%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johannite-ea9b.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q3705019","formula":"Fe(UO₂)₂(SO₄)₂(OH)₂·7H₂O","names":{"en":"Deliensite","uk":"Делієнсит"},"elements":["H","O","S","Fe","U"],"fame":4,"kind":null},{"id":"Q651700","formula":"Fe₅H₄₂S₆O₄₆","names":{"en":"Copiapite","uk":"Копіапіт"},"elements":["H","O","S","Fe"],"fame":18,"kind":null},{"id":"Q417192","formula":"MgFe(SO₄)₂(OH)·7H₂O","names":{"en":"Botryogen","uk":"Ботріоген"},"elements":["H","O","Mg","S","Fe"],"fame":13,"kind":null},{"id":"Q197005","formula":"Cu(UO₂